│    prompts/messages, but again, no explicit model parameter is     │
│    seen in the snippet.                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • The bug is that GPT-4 is not used by default—only GPT-3.5 is    │
│    used unless the --gpt3only flag is set.                         │
│  • The create_chat_completion in the API manager can accept the    │
│    model parameter, but if the callers do not specify the model    │
│    explicitly, or always pass fast_llm_model (GPT-3.5), then GPT-4 │
│    would never be used by default.                                 │
│  • Since the Agent and AgentManager call create_chat_completion    │
│    without model argument, it suggests the model parameter is      │
│    either defaulting internally or passed via some other           │
│    mechanism, which might default to GPT-3.5.                      │
│  • Therefore, the flow from configuration (smart_llm_model = GPT-4 │
│    by default, and fast_llm_model = GPT-3.5) through the agent     │
│    call stack does not culminate in passing GPT-4 as the default   │
│    model to the API manager.                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • The Agent and AgentManager methods should obtain the correct    │
│    LLM model from configuration, respecting any flags (--gpt3only  │
│    or --gpt4only), and explicitly pass the model parameter to      │
│    create_chat_completion.                                         │
│  • The create_chat_completion function in the API manager should   │
│    then use the passed model parameter to direct the OpenAI API    │
│    call accordingly.                                               │
│  • This ensures the use of GPT-4 models by default unless          │
│    overridden, aligning with user expectations and the described   │
│    issue.                                                          │
